{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And Joseph recognized, etc.</b> That is, although he recognized them — given that he left them in the state of youth, and human nature is such that when knowledge is born in the heart of one of two parties, an aspect of memory is also aroused in the heart of the other, for hearts tell hidden secrets, as they said (Proverbs 27:19) ״כַּמַּיִם הַפָּנִים לַפָּנִים כֵּן לֵב הָאָדָם לָאָדָם״ — and they would examine closely with the eyes, the forehead, the speech, and the knowledge would grow greater and greater until the scrutiny was complete — even so, the verse informs us that they did not recognize him. And the reason is that upon seeing him at the height of the ranks, they foreclosed the examination and banished from their hearts the thought of this matter."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:47:57.345057120Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}